{"parentUuid":"50aa0b1e-42fe-4f74-ac30-23134afa1fb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvQPuBd2vtABvgjbYsGA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"F9 is done and the tray works, but the Dock icon fix is untested. It shows only after you rebuild and restart the desktop.\n\n**F9 is done, recorded in PLAN.md (`02dfd2d`):**\n- **The notification showed:** you saw it when j33b65192's plan came to wait.\n- **The tray's count was right:** the menu bar showed the castle with \"2\", matching the server's two waiting jobs.\n- **The plan was approved:** j33b65192 went on to build. I then stopped it for you, since it was a test job.\n- **The desktop started the tray** this time, and `tray.log` stayed empty.\n- **Not run live:** the chat webhook, because none was set. A test posts a notice to a local listener.\n\n**The Dock icon (`538a640`):** macOS gives the Dock's generic \"exec\" tile to a binary that runs outside an app bundle, and the window icon doesn't reach the Dock. On macOS the desktop now hands AppKit the castle as the app's icon when it starts, using the Objective-C bindings already in the lockfile.\n\n**To see it:** run `! cargo build -p bastion-desktop` and restart the window. The castle replaces the \"exec\" tile a moment after launch. A packaged `Bastion.app`, which F10 will build, would show it from the very start.\n\nThere are 10 commits since `fe3f365`, none pushed yet. Next in the plan is F10, packaging and updates."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":222,"cache_read_input_tokens":752478,"output_tokens":471,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":471,"cache_read_input_tokens":752478,"cache_creation_input_tokens":222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"49efef37-707e-4a9f-85de-d2711fa0bf32","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvQPtCLV1xLNjWShzbdx","type":"assistant","uuid":"e75abda7-1135-4b20-8233-a30a75941c36","timestamp":"2026-11-11T03:08:16.690Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
