{"parentUuid":"b37fa4c1-7ae3-4c2b-8e4e-6a447e4c2b9f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/scripts/package.sh","snippet":"42\tcase \"$target\" in\n43\t  *apple-darwin)\n44\t    app=\"$stage/Bastion.app/Contents\"\n45\t    mkdir -p \"$app/MacOS\" \"$app/Resources\"\n46\t    cp \"$rel/bastion-desktop\" \"$rel/bastion-tray\" \"$rel/bastion-server\" \"$rel/bastion\" \"$app/MacOS/\"\n47\t    cp assets/icon/bastion.icns \"$app/Resources/\"\n48\t    sed \"s/@VERSION@/$version/g\" scripts/Info.plist > \"$app/Info.plist\"\n49\t    stack \"$app\"\n50\t    # Ad hoc, until a Developer ID signs it: Apple Silicon runs nothing unsigned,\n51\t    # and a bundle is signed whole.\n52\t    codesign --force --deep --sign - \"$stage/Bastion.app\"\n53\t    (cd \"$stage\" && zip -qry \"$OLDPWD/$out/bastion-desktop-$version-$target.zip\" Bastion.app)\n54\t    ;;\n55\t  *linux*)\n56\t    desk=\"$stage/bastion-desktop-$version\"\n57\t    mkdir -p \"$desk/bin\" \"$desk/share/applications\" \"$desk/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps\"\n58\t    cp \"$rel/bastion-desktop\" \"$rel/bastion-tray\" \"$rel/bastion-server\" \"$rel/bastion\" \"$desk/bin/\"\n59\t    cp scripts/bastion.desktop \"$desk/share/applications/\"\n60\t    cp assets/icon/bastion-256.png \"$desk/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/bastion.png\""},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c42bb472-56cb-42f4-add8-1e7981d003ab","timestamp":"2026-11-11T03:16:28.116Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/scripts/package.sh changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n42\tcase \"$target\" in\n43\t  *apple-darwin)\n44\t    app=\"$stage/Bastion.app/Contents\"\n45\t    mkdir -p \"$app/MacOS\" \"$app/Resources\"\n46\t   