{"parentUuid":"378a4bad-4083-4659-a2eb-d4118f509ee7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvRLhtkKXPwATRZa4jCx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_read_input_tokens":804284,"output_tokens":1174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":336},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":804284,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0ab6b6dd-61b2-4857-82ed-7f9202482cc4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvRLhatwD3BHnzgtwhww","type":"assistant","uuid":"da9ff45c-3b37-4f62-b3c5-f665a18e88e6","timestamp":"2026-11-11T03:20:45.854Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"da9ff45c-3b37-4f62-b3c5-f665a18e88e6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvRLhtkKXPwATRZa4jCx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI passed on both macOS and Ubuntu, including the new Linux packages step for the tray.\n\nF10's code is in place. The rest depends on two things only you can do, so the private key never passes through me.\n\n**1. Make the release key.** Run these yourself:\n```\n! brew install minisign\n! minisign -G -W -p scripts/minisign.pub -s ~/.minisign/bastion.key\n! gh secret set MINISIGN_SECRET_KEY --repo tacoda/bastion < ~/.minisign/bastion.key\n```\n`-W` makes a key with no password, so CI can sign without anyone typing one. The first command replaces the placeholder in `scripts/minisign.pub`. That file holds only the public half, so I can then commit it and put the same key into `install.sh`.\n\n**2. Create the tap repository:** `! gh repo create tacoda/homebrew-bastion --public`\n\n**Once both are done, I will:**\n1. Commit the public key.\n2. Push, and then, with your go-ahead, tag `v0.1.0`. A tag is public, and the workflow publishes a GitHub release.\n3. Check the release and try `curl … | sh` against it.\n4. Write the Homebrew formula (server and CLI) and cask (`Bastion.app`) with the release's checksums, and push them to the tap.\n5. Update the gh-pages site, with `install.sh` served from it.\n\n**Committed since the push:**\n- `e93421c`, F10a: an installed Bastion runs its stack from `share/bastion`, and keeps its data in the user's data folder.\n- `0f81a02`, F10b: `scripts/package.sh` and a release workflow for a `v*` tag. Locally it built both macOS files, and their contents matched the plan.\n- `ee2a2f8`, F10c: `install.sh`, with `--desktop`, `--service` (a systemd user service on Linux), `--version` and `--prefix`.\n- `2bbed34`, F10e: `bastion update`.\n\nNone of these are pushed. Three things haven't run yet: a real release, an install from it, and an update. `install.sh` has only passed a syntax check.\n\n**Limits:**\n- macOS builds are ad-hoc signed only, so a downloaded `Bastion.app` needs one right-click Open, and the cask needs `--no-quarantine`.\n- `install.sh` checks the signature only when `minisign` is installed. It always checks the sums.\n- iii 0.25.0 still has to be installed separately. The installer says so, and the doctor gives the fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_read_input_tokens":804284,"output_tokens":1174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":336},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":804284,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0ab6b6dd-61b2-4857-82ed-7f9202482cc4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgvRLhatwD3BHnzgtwhww","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f14cbaa-5294-4d5f-871c-fb1b8eb2d959","timestamp":"2026-11-11T03:20:46.334Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
