{"parentUuid":"9af98c50-d472-44dc-adba-5f35624de4f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvRYnmmunLYfFQgedCQd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I pushed the four F10 commits. All CI steps passed with no failing test, and `origin/main` is at `2bbed34`.\n\nThe release waits on the key. Please run these yourself, as the account that owns `tacoda/bastion`. The private key never passes through me.\n\n```\n! brew install minisign\n! minisign -G -W -p scripts/minisign.pub -s ~/.minisign/bastion.key\n! gh secret set MINISIGN_SECRET_KEY --repo tacoda/bastion < ~/.minisign/bastion.key\n```\n\nThe `gh` login in this session is `ianparo`, which can't read `tacoda/bastion`'s secrets. So the last command has to run as `tacoda`. Alternatively, paste the key file's contents into the repository's Settings → Secrets → Actions, as `MINISIGN_SECRET_KEY`.\n\nThen say \"continue\". I'll check the public key, commit it with `install.sh`, tag `v0.1.0`, and watch the release workflow. After that I'll test `curl … | sh` against the release, write the Homebrew formula and cask for `tacoda/homebrew-bastion`, and update the gh-pages site."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180,"cache_read_input_tokens":808316,"output_tokens":390,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":180,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":390,"cache_read_input_tokens":808316,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":180},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequ