{"parentUuid":"a5124267-e787-4b60-9112-6715349d2689","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvTRTDpLeNCk9ZW3ixfc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That was by design: `brew install tacoda/bastion/bastion` installs the formula, which holds only the server and the CLI. The window comes from the cask.\n\nI've reworked the cask so the two fit together:\n- It depends on the formula, so `bastion` and `bastion-server` are installed once, by the formula.\n- It links `bastion-desktop` into your PATH.\n- It installs `Bastion.app` in Applications, so Spotlight and the Dock work too.\n\nThe tap is pushed (`bcfd774`), and so is the matching `brew.sh` in Bastion (`e865908`). To get the window, run:\n```\n! brew install --cask --no-quarantine tacoda/bastion/bastion\n```\n\n**F10 is done and recorded in PLAN.md (`1e420f7`). Everything is pushed.**\n- **The release:** v0.1.0 built on all three platforms, and its signed `SHA256SUMS` verified against the release key.\n- **The install script:** `install.sh` installed into a scratch prefix, and the installed CLI ran. `bastion update` found v0.1.0 to be the newest release, and `--desktop` installed a validly signed `Bastion.app`.\n- **The tap:** `tacoda/homebrew-bastion` is live, and your formula install worked.\n- **The site:** it's published, with the curl and Homebrew install commands, the tray, and an \"after the merge\" section. `tacoda.github.io/bastion` redirects to `www.tacoda.dev/bastion/`, and `curl -fsSL` follows the redirect to the new `install.sh`. My edits pass the voice gate. The one staccato run it reports was already on the page.\n\n**Not run yet:**\n- `--service` on a VM,\n- an update across two releases,\n- a Linux install,\n- the cask install, which is the command above.\n\nNext in the plan is F11, the browser agent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_read_input_tokens":854233,"output_tokens":658,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":41},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":658,"cache_read_input_tokens":854233,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7cfc6e87-3f7a-4239-bc7b-b42feb0655a4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgvTRSr1SL9CfSGF65a6H","attributionSkill":"voice-check","type":"assistant","uuid":"e6b9572f-89b2-4a1b-8b44-4d597f52bd23","timestamp":"2026-11-11T03:48:00.703Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
