{"parentUuid":"76f17a7b-50dd-46a5-bfce-98e7e343be0c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvU7zz9S7twhgupvdjaV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dev server and its stack are stopped. I sent TERM to PID 70580, it shut down cleanly, and ports 49190 and 49160 are free. I also removed the pointer file I'd written, since it named the stopped server's folder.\n\n**Open Bastion from Applications now.** It will start its own server from the bundle, which then starts the stack. The first start takes longer than an attach.\n\nOne thing to watch: the installed app's data folder has an old audit anchor from November 7, and the stack's database also holds the newer audit entries from the dev server. If Doctor or the Audit Log reports an anchor mismatch, tell me. That would be the cause.\n\nOne flaw remains in today's pointer fix. A pointer can go stale if a server is later started some other way, and a client would then read the wrong token. I'll make the client try the pointer's token and fall back to its own folder if the server refuses it.\n\nF11 is paused while the stack restarts. Before it stopped, I couldn't list the engine's functions: the console call timed out, and I had a wrong flag for `iii trigger`. Once your app's stack is up, I'll check which sandbox images and browser functions are available and propose the F11 design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_read_input_tokens":876172,"output_tokens":815,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":433},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":815,"cache_read_input_tokens":876172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f328a600-3194-459d-8041-9ac7791a1f9c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgvU7ze4TYsE41pKsBHYY","type":"assistant","uuid":"4600f5f0-eece-49b5-b0ff-a6920ca1c827","timestamp":"2026-11-11T03:57:12.750Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
