{"parentUuid":"cad843c5-fc65-4ef3-a9c3-d9f43913be90","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvUMVdBcptK9a85qxur3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, the server wasn't the cause. The timestamps show it was quick:\n- The window and the server both started at 21:58:52.\n- The server was serving on port 49190 by 21:58:54, two seconds in.\n- The stack was running by 21:59:00. Its database came up just after that.\n\nThe delay was most likely how I started it. I launched the window from a background shell, so macOS didn't bring it to the front. It opened behind your other windows, and you saw it once it surfaced. Opened from Finder or the Dock, macOS brings it forward.\n\nIf a Finder launch is still slow, tell me and I'll time each step of it.\n\nAlso committed: `2a3eaa5`. A server that an app opened from Finder starts now finds `iii`, because the client adds `~/.local/bin` and Homebrew's folders to its `PATH`. This, and the token pointer in `949d25a`, reach the installed app only in the next release. Neither is pushed yet.\n\nNext I'll continue with F11, now that the app's stack is up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1365,"cache_read_input_tokens":883767,"output_tokens":542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":213},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1365,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":542,"cache_read_input_tokens":883767,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1365},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6241c2a1-b888-4ee3-