{"parentUuid":"47cb081a-4177-48ea-a864-db2840588c04","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f754b4dc-5b79-4a86-b45d-8864aa68961f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019QZ47bnRf3oG1iX6Ft5mZZ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```shell\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nraw=open('/tmp/fns.json').read()\ns=min([x for x in (raw.find('{'),raw.find('[')) if x>=0])\nd=json.loads(raw[s:])\nfound=[]\ndef walk(o):\n    if isinstance(o,dict):\n        if o.get('function_id') in ('sandbox::create','sandbox::catalog::list','sandbox::run'): found.append(o)\n        for v in o.values(): walk(v)\n    elif isinstance(o,list):\n        for x in o: walk(x)\nwalk(d)\nfor f in found:\n    print('==', f.get('function_id'))\n    print((f.get('description') or '')[:600])\n    sch=f.get('request_format') or f.get('request_schema') or f.get('input_schema') or f.get('request')\n    print(json.dumps(sch)[:1500] if sch else {k:str(v)[:200] for k,v in f.items() if k!='function_id'})\nEOF\n```\n\n== sandbox::catalog::list\nList bootable images: bundled presets plus operator-registered custom_images. Call this before sandbox::create when you don't know what's available.\n{'description': \"List bootable images: bundled presets plus operator-registered custom_images. Call this before sandbox::create when you don't know what's available.\", 'namespace': 'default', 'worker_name': 'iii-sandbox'}\n== sandbox::create\nCreate an ephemeral sandbox VM. `image` must be a preset (`\"python\"`, `\"node\"`) or a key from `engine.workers.iii-sandbox.custom_images`; OCI refs are NOT accepted unless they match a catalog key. `env` accepts both `Vec<\"K=V\">` and `{ K: V }` map shapes.\n{'description': 'Create an ephemeral sandbox VM. `image` must be a preset (`\"python\"`, `\"node\"`) or a key from `engine.workers.iii-sandbox.custom_images`; OCI refs are NOT accepted unless they match a catalog key. `en', 'namespace': 'default', 'worker_name': 'iii-sandbox'}\n== sandbox::run\nRun code in an ephemeral sandbox in ONE call. Composes create + fs::write + exec + stop. `lang` selects the interpreter (`node`, `python`, `shell`, or a custom binary path). Sandbox auto-stops on success and on failure unless `keep_sandbox: true`. Example: { image: \"node\", code: \"console.log('hi')\", lang: \"node\" }\n{'description': 'Run code in an ephemeral sandbox in ONE call. Composes create + fs::write + exec + stop. `lang` selects the interpreter (`node`, `python`, `shell`, or a custom binary path). Sandbox auto-stops on succ', 'namespace': 'default', 'worker_name': 'iii-sandbox'}\n"}]}]},"uuid":"e0851f46-a63d-46e3-a25c-4e2bd6e4f8ea","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:01:21.586Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"```shell\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nraw=open('/tmp/fns.json').read()\ns=min([x for x in (raw.find('{'),raw.find('[')) if x>=0])\nd=json.loads(raw[s:])\nfound=[]\ndef walk(o):\n    if isinstance(o,dict):\n        if o.get('function_id') in ('sandbox::create','sandbox::catalog::list','sandbox::run'): found.append(o)\n        for v in o.values(): walk(v)\n    elif isinstance(o,list):\n        for x in o: walk(x)\nwalk(d)\nfor f in found:\n    print('==', f.get('function_id'))\n    print((f.get('description') or '')[:600])\n    sch=f.get('request_format') or f.get('request_schema') or f.get('input_schema') or f.get('request')\n    print(json.dumps(sch)[:1500] if sch else {k:str(v)[:200] for k,v in f.items() if k!='function_id'})\nEOF\n```\n\n== sandbox::catalog::list\nList bootable images: bundled presets plus operator-registered custom_images. Call this before sandbox::create when you don't know what's available.\n{'description': \"List bootable images: bundled presets plus operator-registered custom_images. Call this before sandbox::create when you don't know what's available.\", 'namespace': 'default', 'worker_name': 'iii-sandbox'}\n== sandbox::create\nCreate an ephemeral sandbox VM. `image` must be a preset (`\"python\"`, `\"node\"`) or a key from `engine.workers.iii-sandbox.custom_images`; OCI refs are NOT accepted unless they match a catalog key. `env` accepts both `Vec<\"K=V\">` and `{ K: V }` map shapes.\n{'description': 'Create an ephemeral sandbox VM. `image` must be a preset (`\"python\"`, `\"node\"`) or a key from `engine.workers.iii-sandbox.custom_images`; OCI refs are NOT accepted unless they match a catalog key. `en', 'namespace': 'default', 'worker_name': 'iii-sandbox'}\n== sandbox::run\nRun code in an ephemeral sandbox in ONE call. Composes create + fs::write + exec + stop. `lang` selects the interpreter (`node`, `python`, `shell`, or a custom binary path). Sandbox auto-stops on success and on failure unless `keep_sandbox: true`. Example: { image: \"node\", code: \"console.log('hi')\", lang: \"node\" }\n{'description': 'Run code in an ephemeral sandbox in ONE call. Composes create + fs::write + exec + stop. `lang` selects the interpreter (`node`, `python`, `shell`, or a custom binary path). Sandbox auto-stops on succ', 'namespace': 'default', 'worker_name': 'iii-sandbox'}\n"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"65a3e57e-de74-4277-9ae6-0a9d87f1f727","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"47cb081a-4177-48ea-a864-db2840588c04","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
