{"parentUuid":"ecf0d96c-6cdb-451c-80c9-2847fa85e8f7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f754b4dc-5b79-4a86-b45d-8864aa68961f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sb1bUWxCmt4dJUCgf84H9b","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\n| `custom_images` | map | `{}` | Deployment-specific images beyond the built-in presets. Map key is the name used in `image_allowlist` and the `image` field on `sandbox::create`; value is a fully-qualified OCI reference (e.g. `ghcr.io/acme/my-app:1.2.3`). Preset names (`python`, `node`) are reserved. See `docs/api-reference/sandbox.mdx`. |\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\n| `image_allowlist` | string[] | `[]` | **Fail-closed** list of image names that may be booted. Entries must be preset names (`python`, `node`) or keys from `custom_images`. Empty list denies everything — `sandbox::create` returns `S100` for every request. |\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Sample engine configuration for sandbox worker\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\nYAML configuration for the iii-sandbox worker. Adjust image_allowlist and custom_images to control bootable images. Restart the managed Compose invocation after changing engine settings.\n\n```yaml\nengine:\n  workers:\n    iii-sandbox:\n      auto_install: true\n      image_allowlist:\n        - python\n        - node\n      default_idle_timeout_secs: 300\n      max_concurrent_sandboxes: 32\n      max_concurrent_exec_per_sandbox: 4\n      max_exec_timeout_ms: 300000\n      default_cpus: 1\n      default_memory_mb: 512\n\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Sample Configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\n## Sample Configuration\n\n```yaml\nengine:\n  workers:\n    iii-sandbox:\n      auto_install: true\n      image_allowlist:\n        - python\n        - node\n      default_idle_timeout_secs: 300\n      max_concurrent_sandboxes: 32\n      max_concurrent_exec_per_sandbox: 4\n      max_exec_timeout_ms: 300000\n      default_cpus: 1\n      default_memory_mb: 512\n```\n\nTrim or extend `image_allowlist` and `custom_images` to control what callers can boot. Restart the\nmanaged Compose invocation after changing `engine:`.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### sandbox::catalog::list\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\nList the images this engine can boot — bundled presets plus operator-registered custom_images. Empty payload required.\n\n```APIDOC\n## sandbox::catalog::list\n\n### Description\nList the images this engine can boot — bundled presets plus operator-registered `custom_images`. Call it before `sandbox::create` / `sandbox::run` when you don't already know what's available (closes the `S100` \"image not in catalog\" loop).\n\n### Trigger\n`iii.trigger({ function_id: \"sandbox::catalog::list\", payload: {}, timeoutMs })`\n\n### Parameters\n#### Payload Fields\nNone. Empty payload (`{}`).\n\n### Response\n#### Success Response\nReturns: `{ images: [ { name, oci_ref, kind } ] }` where `name` is the value you pass to `image`, `oci_ref` is the pulled reference, and `kind` is `\"preset\"` or `\"custom\"`. Presets come first; custom entries follow, sorted by name.\n```"}]}]},"uuid":"f8c8b87b-31be-41be-9889-0a18bee7af6e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:01:52.810Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"### Configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\n| `custom_images` | map | `{}` | Deployment-specific images beyond the built-in presets. Map key is the name used in `image_allowlist` and the `image` field on `sandbox::create`; value is a fully-qualified OCI reference (e.g. `ghcr.io/acme/my-app:1.2.3`). Preset names (`python`, `node`) are reserved. See `docs/api-reference/sandbox.mdx`. |\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\n| `image_allowlist` | string[] | `[]` | **Fail-closed** list of image names that may be booted. Entries must be preset names (`python`, `node`) or keys from `custom_images`. Empty list denies everything — `sandbox::create` returns `S100` for every request. |\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Sample engine configuration for sandbox worker\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\nYAML configuration for the iii-sandbox worker. Adjust image_allowlist and custom_images to control bootable images. Restart the managed Compose invocation after changing engine settings.\n\n```yaml\nengine:\n  workers:\n    iii-sandbox:\n      auto_install: true\n      image_allowlist:\n        - python\n        - node\n      default_idle_timeout_secs: 300\n      max_concurrent_sandboxes: 32\n      max_concurrent_exec_per_sandbox: 4\n      max_exec_timeout_ms: 300000\n      default_cpus: 1\n      default_memory_mb: 512\n\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Sample Configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\n## Sample Configuration\n\n```yaml\nengine:\n  workers:\n    iii-sandbox:\n      auto_install: true\n      image_allowlist:\n        - python\n        - node\n      default_idle_timeout_secs: 300\n      max_concurrent_sandboxes: 32\n      max_concurrent_exec_per_sandbox: 4\n      max_exec_timeout_ms: 300000\n      default_cpus: 1\n      default_memory_mb: 512\n```\n\nTrim or extend `image_allowlist` and `custom_images` to control what callers can boot. Restart the\nmanaged Compose invocation after changing `engine:`.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### sandbox::catalog::list\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/crates/iii-worker/src/sandbox_daemon/README.md\n\nList the images this engine can boot — bundled presets plus operator-registered custom_images. Empty payload required.\n\n```APIDOC\n## sandbox::catalog::list\n\n### Description\nList the images this engine can boot — bundled presets plus operator-registered `custom_images`. Call it before `sandbox::create` / `sandbox::run` when you don't already know what's available (closes the `S100` \"image not in catalog\" loop).\n\n### Trigger\n`iii.trigger({ function_id: \"sandbox::catalog::list\", payload: {}, timeoutMs })`\n\n### Parameters\n#### Payload Fields\nNone. Empty payload (`{}`).\n\n### Response\n#### Success Response\nReturns: `{ images: [ { name, oci_ref, kind } ] }` where `name` is the value you pass to `image`, `oci_ref` is the pulled reference, and `kind` is `\"preset\"` or `\"custom\"`. Presets come first; custom entries follow, sorted by name.\n```"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ec0c282a-ffe7-4b0a-87b4-992f5639e60b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Context7","title":"Context7","icons":[{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.svg","mimeType":"image/svg+xml","sizes":["any"]},{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.png","mimeType":"image/png","sizes":["512x512"]}],"version":"4.5.0","websiteUrl":"https://context7.com","description":"Context7 provides up-to-date documentation and code examples for libraries and frameworks."}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ecf0d96c-6cdb-451c-80c9-2847fa85e8f7","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
