{"parentUuid":"71d6d3a9-ac2d-41e7-aa20-f24748de387e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvUsU4GMRiHNMX9wate7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014dJN9hqKJsqzC3PhA65NYJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef ed(p,pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert s.count(a)==1,(p,a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\ned('worker-compose.yaml',[(\"\"\"      image_allowlist: [python, node]\n\"\"\",\"\"\"      image_allowlist: [python, node, browser]\n      # A workspace set to `browser` boots this (F11): Playwright with\n      # Chromium, Firefox and WebKit, git, Node and ffmpeg, on Ubuntu 24.04.\n      custom_images:\n        browser: mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.65.0-noble\n\"\"\")])\ned('crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs',[\n(\"\"\"        message.push_str(TOOL_GUIDE);\n        message.push_str(\"\\\\n\\\\n\");\"\"\",\"\"\"        message.push_str(TOOL_GUIDE);\n        message.push_str(\"\\\\n\\\\n\");\n        if self.workspace(record).await.is_ok_and(|w| w.vm_image() == \"browser\") {\n            message.push_str(BROWSER_GUIDE);\n        }\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"/// The VM tag a read-only turn's tree is put back to.\"\"\",\"\"\"/// What a turn on the browser image is told it has (F11).\nconst BROWSER_GUIDE: &str = \"\\\\\nThis VM has Playwright with Chromium, Firefox and WebKit, and Node. It has no\nnetwork, so serve the app inside the VM (for example on 127.0.0.1) and point the\nbrowser there. Keep each screenshot (.png) and recording (.webm) you make under\n/work/artifacts; they are kept with the job for the person to see.\\\\n\\\\n\";\n\n/// The VM tag a read-only turn's tree is put back to.\"\"\"),\n])\nEOF\ngrep -n \"const TOOL_GUIDE\" crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs | head -2; CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo build -p bastion-server 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A7 | head","description":"Register the browser image and add the guide",