{"parentUuid":"e255a46a-361b-48fb-bbc1-d6c614ab24fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvWVtyL8BUPbUJX2QhzB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NdsxLSy58XzVhL6WSw7h4h","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='crates/bastion-server/src/factory/setup.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''        let env = ws.env_vars()?;\n        let vm =''','''        let mut env = ws.env_vars()?;\n        if image == \"browser\" {\n            // The image's own environment does not reach the VM.\n            env.push(format!(\"PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH={BROWSERS}\"));\n        }\n        let vm =''')\ns=s.replace('''/// Brings the loopback''','''/// Where the browser image keeps Playwright's browsers.\nconst BROWSERS: &str = \"/ms-playwright\";\n/// Brings the loopback''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=s[s.index('const BROWSER_GUIDE'):s.index('/// The VM tag a read-only')]\ns=s.replace(old,'''const BROWSER_GUIDE: &str = \"\\\\\nThis VM has Node and Playwright's Chromium, Firefox and WebKit under\n/ms-playwright, but not the playwright npm package; a workspace whose setup\ninstalls playwright@1.65.0 can drive them from a script and record video.\nWithout it, take a screenshot with\n/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-*/chrome-headless-shell-linux*/chrome-headless-shell\n--no-sandbox --window-size=1280,800 --screenshot=/work/artifacts/home.png URL.\nThe VM has no network, so serve the app on 127.0.0.1, and start the server in\nthe same command as the browser: a background process ends with its command.\nKeep each screenshot (.png) and recording (.webm) under /work/artifacts; they\nare kept with the job for the person to see.\\\\n\\\\n\";\n\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"const BROWSER_GUIDE\" -A12 crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs | head -14","description":"Set browser path env and rewrite the browser guide"},"calle