{"parentUuid":"c198361a-3f45-4719-8dce-4d2a0d95ed27","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"305cbff3-a896-4b01-84bb-b6b3038a90f7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nZTyc75zEwsWCCtgPyTbZ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## start dev server bastion-server target/debug data/server\n\n--- [auto-memory | 2026-11-02 16:36 | user/CLAUDE.md] ---\n### [auto-memory] user/CLAUDE.md\n\nIf you have already written attribution into a message that has not been\ncommitted or posted yet, strip it before proceeding rather than flagging it.\n\n## 6. Writing Under My Name\n\nAnything I publish (blog posts, tacoda.dev pages, talks, Fulcorum copy, book\nchapters, project documentation, READMEs) follows `~/.claude/VOICE.md`. That file\nis the single source of truth for voice, slop detection, and prose rules.\n**Read it before drafting or editing published prose. Do not write from memory\nof it.**\n\nThen run the checks as a chain: `/voice-check <path>` first, because it is\nauthoritative and rewrites nothing; `/humanizer` for tone; `/slopbeth` for slop;\n`/voice-check` again as the gate. Each filter is narrower than the last, and\nneither rewriter may hand back what the authoritative check already rejected.\nAll three report signals; none decides whether the writing is good, and\nover-editing prose that already works is a failure.\n\n--- [auto-memory | 2026-11-10 19:35 | project/CLAUDE.md] ---\n### [auto-memory] project/CLAUDE.md\n\n# CLAUDE.md\n\n## The project\n\nBastion is a server and its clients. [PLAN.md](PLAN.md) holds the decisions\n(cited in code as `PLAN.md D<n>`) and the phases; read §3 and §5 before a\nchange.\n\n- `crates/bastion-core`: the factory's rules, pure. It may depend only on\n  `serde` and `sha2`.\n- `crates/bastion-protocol`: the API's types and routes. Only `serde`.\n- `crates/bastion-server`: the HTTP API, events, the factory adapter, the\n  store, the gate, the audit, the stack. Only `src/engine/` imports `iii-sdk`.\n- `crates/bastion-client`: what every interface uses to reach a server: the\n  server list, the local server's start, the API calls, the event stream.\n  Never `bastion-core` or `iii-sdk`.\n- `crates/bastion-cli`: the `bastion` command line, on `bastion-client`.\n- `crates/bastion-desktop`: the iced client. It reaches a server only through\n  `bastion-client`; never through `bastion-core` or `iii-sdk`.\n- `workers/`: Bastion's own iii workers.\n\n---\n\n## test workspace image browser api.sh PUT workspaces\n\n--- [auto-memory | 2026-11-02 16:36 | user/CLAUDE.md] ---\n### [auto-memory] user/CLAUDE.md\n\nWhen editing existing code:\n- Don't \"improve\" adjacent code, comments, or formatting.\n- Don't refactor things that aren't broken.\n- Match existing style, even if you'd do it differently.\n- If you notice unrelated dead code, mention it - don't delete it.\n\nWhen your changes create orphans:\n- Remove imports/variables/functions that YOUR changes made unused.\n- Don't remove pre-existing dead code unless asked.\n\nThe test: Every changed line should trace directly to the user's request.\n\n## 4. Goal-Driven Execution\n\n**Define success criteria. Loop until verified.**\n\nTransform tasks into verifiable goals:\n- \"Add validation\" → \"Write tests for invalid inputs, then make them pass\"\n- \"Fix the bug\" → \"Write a test that reproduces it, then make it pass\"\n- \"Refactor X\" → \"Ensure tests pass before and after\"\n\nFor multi-step tasks, state a brief plan:\n```\n1. [Step] → verify: [check]\n2. [Step] → verify: [check]\n```\n\nStrong success criteria let you loop independently. Weak criteria (\"make it work\") require constant clarification.\n\n--- [auto-memory | 2026-11-10 19:35 | project/CLAUDE.md] ---\n### [auto-memory] project/CLAUDE.md\n\nRun `pre_commit_code_health_safeguard` and commit only when it passes. After\nchanging code, run `code_health_review` on the changed files, and if Code\nHealth drops, fix it and confirm with `code_health_score`.\n\n## Before a push\n\nRun every CI step, not only the tests:\n\n```sh\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\nscripts/check-seams.sh\ncargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings\ncargo test --workspace\n```\n\n> Throttle: call #1/8 in this window. 2 call(s) before soft cap. Prefer ctx_search(queries: [...]) array form for multi-query workloads — it counts as a single call."}]}]},"uuid":"436b11a3-703e-4c8d-8a3b-2c785690b8b7","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:29:13.546Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"## start dev server bastion-server target/debug data/server\n\n--- [auto-memory | 2026-11-02 16:36 | user/CLAUDE.md] ---\n### [auto-memory] user/CLAUDE.md\n\nIf you have already written attribution into a message that has not been\ncommitted or posted yet, strip it before proceeding rather than flagging it.\n\n## 6. Writing Under My Name\n\nAnything I publish (blog posts, tacoda.dev pages, talks, Fulcorum copy, book\nchapters, project documentation, READMEs) follows `~/.claude/VOICE.md`. That file\nis the single source of truth for voice, slop detection, and prose rules.\n**Read it before drafting or editing published prose. Do not write from memory\nof it.**\n\nThen run the checks as a chain: `/voice-check <path>` first, because it is\nauthoritative and rewrites nothing; `/humanizer` for tone; `/slopbeth` for slop;\n`/voice-check` again as the gate. Each filter is narrower than the last, and\nneither rewriter may hand back what the authoritative check already rejected.\nAll three report signals; none decides whether the writing is good, and\nover-editing prose that already works is a failure.\n\n--- [auto-memory | 2026-11-10 19:35 | project/CLAUDE.md] ---\n### [auto-memory] project/CLAUDE.md\n\n# CLAUDE.md\n\n## The project\n\nBastion is a server and its clients. [PLAN.md](PLAN.md) holds the decisions\n(cited in code as `PLAN.md D<n>`) and the phases; read §3 and §5 before a\nchange.\n\n- `crates/bastion-core`: the factory's rules, pure. It may depend only on\