{"parentUuid":"eed9b41f-01ca-45bd-9cd5-041a3c4343ee","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01QDJYeqPrhwbpY522yzgMtg","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"af169034-adf2-42ce-9172-cdf20c334b2c","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:35:19.664Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"af169034-adf2-42ce-9172-cdf20c334b2c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvX2sPSsxVn2sawvW9S8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"F11 is done and pushed, as 4 commits. `origin/main` is now at `4bb2089`. Before the push, fmt, the seam check, clippy and the full test suite all passed.\n\n**What changed in the last commit (`60e5296`)**\n- **Loopback:** an offline VM booted with `lo` down, so nothing could be served on 127.0.0.1. The images have no `ip` command, so the factory now uses Perl to bring `lo` up in every new VM. If that fails, the factory logs it and the VM still boots. I tested it in a live VM. With `lo` down, a request to a local server timed out. After the fix, the same request got its answer.\n- **Browser path:** the image's own environment does not reach the VM. So the factory now sets `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/ms-playwright` on browser VMs.\n- **Turn instructions:** browser turns are now told the exact screenshot command that works offline. They are also told to start a local server in the same command as the browser, because a background process stops when its command ends.\n\n**Live test on DeepSeek:** I made a small static-site workspace, `demo-browser`, on the browser image and submitted a test job. The agent added a paragraph, served the site with node, and took a screenshot. The factory kept `home.png` on the job, and `GET /jobs/j05ebb3a9/media/home.png` serves it: 1280×800, with the new paragraph showing.\n\n**Not tested live:**\n- a video recording\n- a workspace whose setup installs the playwright npm package to run a browser script\n- the \"Kept files\" section on the desktop job page\n\nPLAN.md records these gaps.\n\n**Actions I took as you:**\n- I restarted the dev server (PID 2198) on the new build.\n- I added the `demo-browser` workspace.\n- I approved the plan of test job `j05ebb3a9`.\n\nThat job now waits at build for your approval. You can approve it or leave it.\n\nStill open from before:\n- The old installed server (PID 94604) is still running. To stop it, run `! kill -9 94604`.\n- Release v0.1.1 would give the installed app the fixes in `949d25a` and `2a3eaa5`, which v0.1.0 does not have. Say if you want it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":313,"cache_read_input_tokens":137549,"output_tokens":736,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":313,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":736,"cache_read_input_tokens":137549,"cache_creation_input_tokens":313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":313},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d3eb5260-f49a-4ea6-ae5b-6afff72217c1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgvX2rtvhziuJiosSJFD1","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b4f1735-d72d-4a22-a274-e6706cd71caf","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:35:19.663Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
