{"parentUuid":"893f5194-ec93-4193-bde3-ee145a8b519b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvYg2RpAePtyXQMdCBEP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I tested the two remaining F11 gaps live, and both work. The PLAN.md note is updated and pushed (`c847db8`).\n\n- **A workspace whose setup installs playwright:** I gave the `demo-browser` workspace the setup command `npm install --no-save --no-audit --no-fund playwright@1.65.0`. The setup ran in its own VM with the network, and the agent's offline VM then had playwright. The installed `node_modules` did not get into the agent's commits.\n- **A recording:** test job `j7193587d` wrote and ran a Playwright script. The script served the site and recorded Chromium clicking a new \"Back to top\" link. The factory kept `visit.webm` (25 KB) and `after.png` on the job, and the media route served both. I looked at a frame from the video and at the screenshot, and both show the new link.\n\n**Actions I took as you, all on test jobs in the scratch repo:**\n- I approved the build and the land for `j05ebb3a9`, so its change landed there.\n- I set the setup command above on `demo-browser`.\n- I approved the plan for `j7193587d`. That job now waits at build for your approval.\n\n**Still open:**\n- I have not looked at the \"Kept files\" section of the desktop job page with a live job.\n- PLAN.md §7 has four open questions: dark to merge, configuration in git, multi-user hosting, and unused stack workers. Each one is your decision.\n- Release v0.1.1 would give the installed app the pointer fix and the PATH fix. Say if you want it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":150945,"output_tokens":526,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache