{"parentUuid":"e9d004b3-18a7-4553-a6ab-1b58df72a482","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwQDRwkacutbBegwZ9JJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't cancel or rerun the runs. GitHub answered `HTTP 403: Must have admin rights to Repository` for both.\n\nI'll hold the `v0.1.1` tag for now, because the release workflow runs the same apt step on its Linux builds. Both CI runs are stuck in \"Linux packages\" (`sudo apt-get update` and `apt-get install`) for about an hour, and the code checks have not started. The macOS job of run `43041563436` passed.\n\nPlease cancel both runs and rerun the newer one, in the Actions tab or with an admin login:\n\n```\n! gh run cancel 43040265803; gh run cancel 43041563436\n! gh run rerun 43041563436\n```\n\nWhen it passes, I'll tag `v0.1.1`, wait for the release, and update the Homebrew tap.\n\nIf you want, I can also add a `timeout-minutes` to the apt step in `ci.yml` and `release.yml`. Then a hung mirror fails in minutes instead of running up to GitHub's 6-hour limit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":194865,"output_tokens":542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":203},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":568,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":542,"cache_read_input_tokens":194865,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":568},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"36830145-7baa-48b1-886e-9e3363aab029","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwQDRmLPD2VYyokJnBU6","ty